
	-----------------
	1) INFLUENCE
	-----------------
	1.1) Influence is NOT about adjusting behavior
		- It is about controlling/commanding reality
		- Can never dictate it; must live it
	1.2) Influence breaks/modifies a person's reality
	1.3) Influence is about WHO you are and WHAT you are when you say those words
		- You command your own reality
	1.4) Ways people categorize other's behavior:
		1.4.1) People are Broken - people have pathologies
		1.4.2) People are Different - personality tests/ego battles
		1.4.3) People are Data/Facts
		1.4.4) People are Reasons - Motivations/Wounds behind the facts
		1.4.5) People are Reflections - Parallellize/project/empathize the influencer's traits
	1.5) Succesful influencers fall into 1.4.4) and 1.4.5)
	1.6) Confidence is about elimination of veneers
	-----------------
	-----------------
	2) READING PEOPLE
	-----------------
	2.1) Major Initial Influence - Childhood Experience
		- Positives/Negatives => Punishment/Rewards
	2.2) Facets of Human Values:
		2.2.1) Six Social Needs
		2.2.2) How do I make decisions
		2.2.3) What do I represent (my epitaph/tombstone)
	2.3) Six Childhood Social Needs - not physical/material/emotional needs
		2.3.1) Significance => Need to feel significant - manage 100s of teams
		2.3.2) Acceptance => Use terms like we/us/teams/groups, memberships etc. | Need to belong
		2.3.3) Approval => seek permission/reassurance
		2.3.4) Intelligence => want to acknowledge my intelligence
		2.3.5) Pity => want us to understand their journey/how they have been a hero
		2.3.6) Strength => Posturing
	-----------------
	-----------------
	3) Trusts
	-----------------
	3.1) Asset Transfers happen by (precedence):
		- Beneficiary Designation
		- Contract/Title Transfer
		- Trust Designate
			- Trust Grantor transfers assets to a trustee to be managed for beneficiaries according to grantor's rules
			- Beneficiary can also be a trustee
			- Privacy, no probate proceedings
			- Trust can be living concurrent with the donor
			- Revocable trust no probate during incapacity
			- Revocable/irrevocable trusts allow for custom inheritance rules
			- Irrevocable trust - Trust Grantor gives up control of assets to the trustee
				- Useful for estate tax reduction, medical planning, advanced wealth transfer strategies
		- Will/Probate
			- Will directs distribution of probate assets - operational only at death
	3.2) None of the above direct avoid taxes (except for irrevocable trust)
